## 5.2 Linked and Independent Components

Support two relationship types.

**Linked Components**
- Physically or geometrically dependent on another building section.
- Their position and relevant geometry update when their parent changes.

**Independent Components**
- Can be positioned and edited independently.
- Must not automatically move with unrelated building components.

Example:
- If an existing ground-floor building section moves, its corresponding upper-floor component follows if configured as linked.
- A separate extension with its own footprint and structural system remains independent.

Provide:
- Link component.
- Unlink component.
- Change parent component.
- Move independently.
- Reset to parent alignment.

